(6468527, 961373, 99263, '<td valign="top">Very nice Ammie. I love the depth in this image. Actually it was quite difficult to find yours this time as there are at least 4 other images in this challenge which look like they could have been taken in the area you live in. This one has your style and signature printed all over it though.</td>', 'Very nice Ammie. I love the depth in this image. Actually it was quite difficult to find yours this time as there are at least 4 other images in this challenge which look like they could have been taken in the area you live in. This one has your style and signature printed all over it though.', '2011-07-12 18:09:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6468669, 961251, 53147, '<td valign="top">Hey David. I voted this a 7. I thought it was a humorous and creative take on the challenge and not what I was expecting to come across - which is a good thing IMO. The out of box thinking doesn''t always garner you high scores, but I would assume you are getting some praiseworthy comments for the idea. Execution wise the lighting may be a bit harsh as the shadows are pretty sharp on your model. I think you could have fared well with a slightly heavy handed edit, making it a tad bit more cartoonish - maybe making the keys a bit more quickly recognizable by appearance rather than just the idea (with them laying flat and the harsh lighting they kind of go blah on the eyes). Your model has a great frustrated look. Overall though I am not sure if there was much you could do editing wise or anything to really effect the score much. The out of the box thinking is probably what is hurting you most - but again that is what I appreciated in this image.</td>', 'Hey David. I voted this a 7. I thought it was a humorous and creative take on the challenge and not what I was expecting to come across - which is a good thing IMO. The out of box thinking doesn''t always garner you high scores, but I would assume you are getting some praiseworthy comments for the idea. Execution wise the lighting may be a bit harsh as the shadows are pretty sharp on your model. I think you could have fared well with a slightly heavy handed edit, making it a tad bit more cartoonish - maybe making the keys a bit more quickly recognizable by appearance rather than just the idea (with them laying flat and the harsh lighting they kind of go blah on the eyes). Your model has a great frustrated look. Overall though I am not sure if there was much you could do editing wise or anything to really effect the score much. The out of the box thinking is probably what is hurting you most - but again that is what I appreciated in this image.', '2011-07-12 22:48:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6469042, 961205, 18073, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colours and a nice balanced composition, really pretty, well done!</td>', 'Beautiful colours and a nice balanced composition, really pretty, well done!', '2011-07-13 04:00:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6469063, 961435, 21714, '<td valign="top">The selective focus creates an interesting perspective. It even appears as if you have placed a little cutout of her in the fence.</td>', 'The selective focus creates an interesting perspective. It even appears as if you have placed a little cutout of her in the fence.', '2011-07-13 04:33:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6469069, 961379, 21714, '<td valign="top">While it''s definitely very far, it does not appear to be. You have reached relatively close to it yet those craters are so far away. the question is if it serves the purpose of the challenge. Perhaps not.</td>', 'While it''s definitely very far, it does not appear to be. You have reached relatively close to it yet those craters are so far away. the question is if it serves the purpose of the challenge. Perhaps not.', '2011-07-13 04:36:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6469075, 961213, 20799, '<td valign="top">OK, where do I start.<br/>This has to be everyone''s 10. Not only because of the historic significance of the last shuttle flight, or for all the beautiful elements of the picture. But most of all, I''d love to see DPC support and live the dream of space exploration.<br/> <br/>If I''m not mistaken, this is the moment when the orbiter enters the "maximum dynamic pressure" region of the atmosphere and the engines throttle down. What follows is "go for throttle up", when it blasts full speed into orbit. I love that you caught this particular moment with the mist around the SRBs. Can''t wait to read your story about this photo.</td>', 'OK, where do I start.This has to be everyone''s 10. Not only because of the historic significance of the last shuttle flight, or for all the beautiful elements of the picture. But most of all, I''d love to see DPC support and live the dream of space exploration. If I''m not mistaken, this is the moment when the orbiter enters the "maximum dynamic pressure" region of the atmosphere and the engines throttle down. What follows is "go for throttle up", when it blasts full speed into orbit. I love that you caught this particular moment with the mist around the SRBs. Can''t wait to read your story about this photo.', '2011-07-13 04:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6469146, 960901, 18073, '<td valign="top">I can imagine this as a huge canvas print, would look great on a wall.  Love the composition and gradient of the light in this photo.  Good luck!</td>', 'I can imagine this as a huge canvas print, would look great on a wall.  Love the composition and gradient of the light in this photo.  Good luck!', '2011-07-13 08:52:13.000000', NULL, 1),
